        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Three-Storey Residence with Views over Blessington Lakes.\r\n\r\nThis impressive three-storey residence extends to approximately 261 sq. m. (2,813 sq. ft.) and occupies an elevated position within a mature and exceptionally scenic setting overlooking Blessington Lakes. Approached by a winding private drive, the property enjoys a wonderful sense of privacy and seclusion, while taking full advantage of the spectacular surrounding countryside and lake views.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is spacious and versatile, offering excellent potential for those seeking a substantial family home, countryside retreat or refurbishment project. The accommodation briefly comprises entrance hall, living room, kitchen/dining room, conservatory, drawing room, studio, five bedrooms, study, playroom and three bathrooms.\r\n\r\nInternally, the property features timber flooring, exposed timber ceilings and traditional fireplaces. The generous proportions and abundance of natural light provide an excellent foundation for modernization, while the existing layout offers considerable scope to reconfigure and personalize the accommodation to suit individual requirements.\r\n\r\nThe house has been unoccupied for a number of years and, subject to the relevant criteria and confirmation from the appropriate authority, it is understood that the property may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant. This presents an exciting opportunity for a purchaser to undertake a comprehensive refurbishment and create a unique home in an enviable rural location.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property is set within generous grounds on c. 1 Acre and benefits from extensive off-street parking. The surrounding gardens incorporate a number of attractive granite stone features, including a granite-surrounded pond which adds further character to the setting. A particularly interesting feature of the grounds is the ruins of the original granite cottage, providing a tangible link to the property's history and adding further interest and potential to the overall holding.\r\n\r\nThe elevated position is undoubtedly one of the property's greatest assets, with views across Blessington Lakes and the surrounding Wicklow countryside. The mature trees and established landscape provide privacy while framing the exceptional outlook.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the setting, scale and potential this property has to offer.\r\n\r\nLOCATION\r\nSituated just off the Lake Drive Road at Ballinastockan, nestled between Lacken and Ballyknockan villages, the location of this property is fantastic. Blessington is a short 10 minute drive away offering all you could want in convenience and leisure. All the amenities of Blessington are on the doorstep and yet Dublin is a short journey away via the N81. Whether you enjoy sports such as sailing, kayaking, walking, GAA or golf, these are all well catered for locally.  With sailing and kayak clubs just a stones throw from the house, horse racing in Punchestown, and hill walking and hiking in the Wicklow mountains, you will never be at a loose end.  There are many good golf courses in the area including Tulfarris Golf Club and Blessington Lakes Golf Club. Not to mention Palmerstown House Golf Club and the renowned K-Club in neighbouring Co. Kildare. Blessington is famous for its warm and friendly village atmosphere and its cafés, pubs and eateries are no exception. The nearby Ballymore Inn has been award winning for any years and the larger town of Naas offers further restaurants, bars, hotels and shopping. Lacken offers a small primary school with an excellent reputation, while Blessington has many primary schools including an all Irish Gaelscoile. For secondary education you could opt for Blessington or Naas Schools or you could easily opt for Terenure College, Our Lady`s, in Terenure, Newbridge College or Clongowes Wood for private Schools.\r\n\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION\r\nENTRANCE HALL\t\t\r\nLIVING ROOM\t5.23m x 4.33m\tWith raised fireplace, vaulted ceiling & gallery overlooking.\r\nKITCHEN\t5.92m x 4.09m\tWith fitted kitchen units, wooden flooring & wood fire burning stove.\r\nDRAWING ROOM / STUDY\t6.62m x 3.08m\tWith built in bookshelves.\r\nBATHROOM 1\t3.68m x 2.79m\tWith bath, W.C & W.H.B.\r\nBEDROOM 1\t3.49m x 3.40m\t\r\nCONSERVATORY\t6.20m x 2.60m\t\r\nFIRST FLOOR\t\t\r\nLANDING\t\t\r\nSTUDIO\t6.02m x 2.62m\t\r\nBEDROOM 2\t4.79m x 2.78m\t\r\nBEDROOM 3\t6.60m x 3.06m\t\r\nBATHROOM 2\t2.50m x 2.16m\tWith bath, W.C & W.H.B.\r\nBEDROOM 4\t3.54m x 2.42m\t\r\nBEDROOM 5\t3.48m x 3.27m\t\r\nSECOND FLOOR\t\t\r\nPLAYROOM\t6.81m x 3.73m\t\r\nBATHROOM 3\t1.83m x 1.25m\tWith W.C & W.H.B.\r\nOFFICE\t4.78m x 2.02m"
      },
